<title>POLAND: Mostostal-W reduces 1996 sales forecast.</title>
<headline>Mostostal-W reduces 1996 sales forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Mostostal Warszawa cut its 1996 sales forecast to 105 million zlotys from earlier predicted 120 million because of a delay in its biggest contract this year, the firm said.</p>
<p>Mostostal Warszawa said in a statement on Friday its 45-million-zloty contract on building an installation for desulphurisation for copper giant KGHM was postponed for six months, which influenced the firm's sales.</p>
<p>It said, however, its net profit was unlikely to be hit by the delay of the contract and maintained its forecast at four million zlotys.</p>
